## Mermaid diagram macro powered by beautiful-mermaid
##
## Admin setup (Confluence Server / Data Center):
##   1. Management → User Macros → Create User Macro
##   2. Macro name: beautiful-mermaid-confluence
##   3. Icon URL: hosted dist/beautiful-mermaid.icon.png (same static server as the JS)
##   4. Documentation URL: https://github.com/WindieChai/confluence-beautiful-mermaid
##   5. Macro body: Has body
##   6. Body processing: Unrendered
##   7. Output: HTML
##   8. Paste this template into the User Macro only (not Custom HTML)
##   9. Custom HTML → At end of BODY must be ONLY the two script lines:
##        window.beautifulMermaidBundleUrl = '.../beautiful-mermaid.bundle.js'
##        <script src=".../beautiful-mermaid.init.js"></script>

## @param theme:title=Theme|type=enum|enumValues=light,dark|default=light|desc=Diagram color theme

<div class="beautiful-mermaid-confluence" data-state="pending" data-theme="$paramtheme">
  <div class="bm-source" hidden style="display:none">$body</div>
  <div class="bm-render-target">Rendering diagram...</div>
</div>
